    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d810">

                <pb facs="1571" n="1531" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v09p1/pg1531"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">674.84A/4–2754: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 810<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Israel (Russell) to the Department of State</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d810-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Tel
                                Aviv</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1954-04-27T13:00:00+02:00">April 27, 1954—1 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1114. Reference Cairo telegram 74 (1348 to Department)<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d810-f2"/> and Embtel 1071 to
                    Department (82 to Cairo).<anchor n="3" xml:id="d810-f3"/></p>
                <p>Foreign Ministry informed Embassy this morning: <list>
                        <label>1.</label>
                        <item>Desires meet with Riad though
                            would have no objection to Gohar
                            or other representative also being present.</item>
                        <label>2.</label>
                        <item>IG representatives will be Lt. Colonel
                            Shalev (IDF) and Samuel Divon
                            (recently of Israel Embassy, and currently advisor on Middle East
                            affairs in Foreign Ministry).</item>
                        <label>3.</label>
                        <item>Would prefer meeting without UN
                            observer present but will acquiesce if Riad wishes.</item>
                        <label>4.</label>
                        <item>Latest developments indicate desirability of early meeting and suggest
                            Thursday or even Wednesday (tomorrow).</item>
                        <label>5.</label>
                        <item>Suggests IG be informed through this
                            Embassy of Riad’s wishes as to
                            time and place of rendezvous of cars and place of meeting (presumably
                            Beersheba or Gaza).</item>
                    </list></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Russell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
